// =============================================================================
// Values
// =============================================================================

/// Copies a value a callback delivered - an LE read or notification, a server write
/// request, a Classic chunk - into out_data at offset: all size bytes the callback
/// reported, and frees the value. InvalidHandle for an unknown, fetched, released or
/// expired value; InvalidArgument for a buffer too small for it, which keeps the
/// value. The bytes are written straight into the buffer's memory, so its used size
/// does not change: buffer_set_used_size() before buffer_copy() or buffer_save(), or
