/// is the server characteristic read, or the one descriptor belongs to; descriptor is
/// 0 for a characteristic read. offset is where in the value the central reads from (a
/// long read asks again at later offsets); answer with the bytes from there on, or
/// InvalidOffset past the end. An attribute with a static or initial value is read
/// without reaching on_read, on every platform; Apple never reports a descriptor read.
